WEBVTT


00:00:02.518 --> 00:00:04.247
Wait, wait!


00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.255
You can't do that, man.


00:00:09.491 --> 00:00:11.721
Stand up!
You're stopping the column!


00:00:11.927 --> 00:00:13.519
- Hold my gun.
- Let's go.


00:00:19.735 --> 00:00:22.203
The next letter is...


00:00:23.138 --> 00:00:24.901
No? Look.


00:00:25.073 --> 00:00:27.268
Here. Yello...


00:00:28.143 --> 00:00:31.442
Excuse me, Che.
He says he needs to talk to you.


00:00:31.613 --> 00:00:32.671
What's going on?


00:00:32.848 --> 00:00:36.875
Comandante, Camilo calls me
a bad word every time he sees me.


00:00:37.052 --> 00:00:39.919
- What bad word?
- Something rude I don't like.


00:00:40.088 --> 00:00:43.057
Go and get Camilo.
Like what?


00:00:43.225 --> 00:00:46.752
I don't want to be a bother, but I'm a man
who shouldn't be disrespected.


00:00:46.962 --> 00:00:48.896
Everyone is laughing
and making fun of me.


00:00:49.131 --> 00:00:52.225
I don't really understand
what he's saying, but I don't like it.


00:00:52.401 --> 00:00:54.869
What's going on, comandante?


00:00:55.037 --> 00:00:56.470
Albertico.


00:00:57.639 --> 00:00:59.266
What's the story?


00:00:59.942 --> 00:01:02.968
Okay, friend, now tell me
what Camilo's been saying to you?


00:01:03.345 --> 00:01:06.644
He calls me "vanilla piss."


00:01:08.617 --> 00:01:11.245
Ventriloquist, man, ventriloquist.


00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.083
- That's not a bad word.
- But it sounds bad. I don't like it.


00:01:15.257 --> 00:01:18.249
A ventriloquist is someone
who talks without moving his mouth.


00:01:20.162 --> 00:01:22.687
- Why are you calling me that?
- Yes, Camilo, why?


00:01:22.865 --> 00:01:25.265
Because he's a good messenger


00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:28.494
and he's always popping up
with information,


00:01:29.004 --> 00:01:33.202
and he reminds me of a ventriloquist
puppet that moves like this.


00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:35.036
Albertico, it's not a bad word.


00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:37.770
It's not an insult, man.
I say it with affection.


00:01:38.013 --> 00:01:40.038
- He's a very good messenger.
- Really?


00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:44.050
No, it's true. He's doing things
really well. He's always there.


00:01:44.219 --> 00:01:45.447
Yes, he is.


00:01:45.621 --> 00:01:47.088
You wanna play ball, Che?


00:01:47.289 --> 00:01:51.885
Today is a perfect day to abandon
the guerrilla movement.


00:01:53.195 --> 00:01:57.325
Another chance like this
may not come along for weeks.


00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:00.532
Let's see.


00:02:01.503 --> 00:02:04.597
Anyone who'd like to leave
this column, step forward.


00:02:17.686 --> 00:02:19.153
Stand up there.


00:02:19.354 --> 00:02:22.653
Come on,
the quitters and the horses' asses!


00:02:26.395 --> 00:02:28.124
Stay there.


00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.732
I'm not leaving because I'm scared.
I have a pain and...


00:02:34.903 --> 00:02:36.962
You are a moron. Shut up.


00:02:37.139 --> 00:02:39.869
- My mother is sick.
- You are a moron!


00:02:42.911 --> 00:02:46.745
You'll have to give back everything
that belongs to the column.


00:02:46.915 --> 00:02:48.906
You're a bunch of cowards.


00:02:49.184 --> 00:02:52.051
You have 30 minutes
to get out of here.


00:02:52.287 --> 00:02:58.749
If we find you, you're deserters.
Israel, Roberto, take them out.


00:03:00.662 --> 00:03:04.291
Dickhead, aren't you leaving with them?


00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.590
Another faggot.


00:03:09.471 --> 00:03:10.938
Anyone else?


00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.574
So did you grow balls?


00:03:19.247 --> 00:03:20.805
We can still stand a little bit more.


00:03:23.118 --> 00:03:25.086
You already behaved with dignity,


00:03:25.253 --> 00:03:29.656
but you have no chance
of adapting to this warfare.


00:03:30.692 --> 00:03:32.717
Okay, I'll make an exception.


00:03:33.629 --> 00:03:37.793
I'll let you take your things with you,
I'll give you a guide


00:03:37.966 --> 00:03:40.457
and 10 pesos to each of you.


00:03:40.969 --> 00:03:42.834
Comandante.


00:03:43.805 --> 00:03:46.239
I think you should
forgive me in advance,


00:03:46.408 --> 00:03:49.070
as I know you will not like
what I'm going to say.


00:03:51.079 --> 00:03:55.448
If we joined the troops,
it wasn't to go back humiliated.


00:03:55.617 --> 00:03:58.643
We prefer, and I speak for both,


00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:02.278
to die on this mountain rather than
return home as failures.


00:04:02.524 --> 00:04:06.051
We'll make the maximum effort
even if it costs our lives.


00:04:06.728 --> 00:04:08.787
This is the last straw.


00:04:09.297 --> 00:04:13.495
While the strong
grow weaker and leave,


00:04:13.669 --> 00:04:16.365
these snot-nosed kids
get more courageous.


00:04:17.239 --> 00:04:19.036
Is there any logic here?


00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:33.046
The important ones aren't the ones
who leave, but the ones who stay


00:04:33.288 --> 00:04:35.347
and the ones
who will join us in the future.


00:04:36.258 --> 00:04:37.623
Listen to me.


00:04:37.993 --> 00:04:40.894
Comandantes Raúl and Almeida
will come with me.


00:04:41.363 --> 00:04:43.991
They will open the second
and third front with their columns.


00:04:44.966 --> 00:04:46.524
Camilo


00:04:47.135 --> 00:04:49.296
will replace Sardinas
as your new captain.


00:04:52.808 --> 00:04:54.207
Damn.


00:04:54.376 --> 00:04:57.106
Look how generous the revolution is.


00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:35.568
Long live free Cuba!


00:06:39.181 --> 00:06:42.480
Will they have much time to respond?


00:06:42.651 --> 00:06:44.516
Each one will have 10 minutes.


00:06:46.688 --> 00:06:50.124
- From the podium?
- No, from the floor.


00:06:51.326 --> 00:06:53.658
- And my rebuttal?
- Ten minutes.


00:06:55.997 --> 00:06:58.795
- Also from the floor?
- No, from the podium.


00:07:01.837 --> 00:07:05.898
My government has nothing to do
with the fact that every day,


00:07:07.275 --> 00:07:11.974
in Cuban circles, to bolster
the illusions of the Cuban people,


00:07:13.181 --> 00:07:17.174
they announce
the formation of invading brigades


00:07:17.352 --> 00:07:19.411
armed with revolvers


00:07:19.621 --> 00:07:23.682
and small-caliber weapons
to confront an army that,


00:07:23.859 --> 00:07:28.023
according to
the declarations of their leaders,


00:07:28.196 --> 00:07:33.691
has at their disposal,
the most modern nuclear arms.


00:08:13.241 --> 00:08:17.610
Absolutely false are the accusations


00:08:17.779 --> 00:08:21.909
that acts of genocide are being
committed in Venezuela.


00:08:22.417 --> 00:08:26.751
Moreover,
it is simply absurd and intolerable


00:08:26.922 --> 00:08:29.186
that a Cuban representative


00:08:29.357 --> 00:08:33.054
dares to make judgments
about Venezuelan sovereignty,


00:08:33.295 --> 00:08:38.130
the unique and exclusive patrimony
of the Venezuelan people,


00:08:38.767 --> 00:08:41.634
a truly free people,


00:08:41.803 --> 00:08:44.237
which has a democratic government


00:08:44.406 --> 00:08:48.137
with elections whose legitimacy
are known to the entire world.


00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:51.541
The tragedy of the Cuban revolution


00:08:51.713 --> 00:08:56.912
lies in not having known how to
institutionalize this great movement


00:08:57.085 --> 00:09:00.145
into an administration
with legal rights in the Americas.


00:09:00.322 --> 00:09:02.882
The greatest flaw of their leaders


00:09:03.091 --> 00:09:07.926
is that they suffer from excessive vanity
which blinds them


00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:11.231
and prevents them
from observing past examples


00:09:11.466 --> 00:09:13.491
which are typical of America,


00:09:13.902 --> 00:09:17.429
like the Mexican revolution in 1910.


00:09:18.773 --> 00:09:23.972
I, who lived many years
of my youth in Cuba,


00:09:24.946 --> 00:09:27.779
and who perhaps
feels more than Che Guevara


00:09:27.983 --> 00:09:30.247
that there has been
enough suffering


00:09:30.418 --> 00:09:32.978
and pain for the Cuban people.


00:09:33.321 --> 00:09:38.122
In my brief reply to your capricious
intervention into Panamanian issues,


00:09:38.326 --> 00:09:41.659
I'd like to finish by saying to you:


00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.594
Don't defend me, compadre.


00:10:27.008 --> 00:10:28.202
Vilo!


00:10:28.376 --> 00:10:30.139
Take the sick to the shelter!


00:10:30.311 --> 00:10:32.211
To the shelter!
Take them to the shelter.


00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:34.348
Don't run. Don't run.


00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.820
Hurry up!


00:10:51.833 --> 00:10:53.266
Come on!


00:11:21.896 --> 00:11:24.091
One, two, three.


00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:32.804
Polo. Take the prisoners
to your house and keep them there.


00:11:34.109 --> 00:11:38.239
Polo. Make sure no one mistreats them,
verbally or physically.


00:11:38.613 --> 00:11:41.081
- Understood, Roberto?
- Sure.


00:11:42.717 --> 00:11:44.116
Come on, walk!


00:11:50.225 --> 00:11:51.419
Che!


00:11:52.994 --> 00:11:56.293
They killed Ciro.
They shot him in the head.


00:11:58.566 --> 00:12:00.193
We couldn't recover his body.


00:12:40.542 --> 00:12:42.533
May I talk to you for a second, sir?


00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:51.041
They were very well organized.


00:12:51.953 --> 00:12:54.581
- More than we expected?
- Much more.


00:12:54.756 --> 00:12:59.693
They have a school, hospital,
printing press, a power plant.


00:12:59.861 --> 00:13:01.829
They must have been here months.


00:13:03.331 --> 00:13:05.060
What do you want me to do with this?


00:13:08.903 --> 00:13:10.268
Torch it.


00:13:14.209 --> 00:13:16.268
I need you to go to Minas del Frío


00:13:16.511 --> 00:13:18.411
and create a training camp.


00:13:20.048 --> 00:13:21.481
What for?


00:13:23.518 --> 00:13:27.852
I want you to be personally
in charge of the new recruits.


00:13:29.724 --> 00:13:31.817
What about my column?


00:13:32.594 --> 00:13:35.188
Ramiro can take your place for now.


00:13:39.367 --> 00:13:41.733
You know we're days away
from an attack.


00:13:44.405 --> 00:13:48.239
- I don't understand.
- This is more important.


00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:52.103
It makes sense, teach.


00:13:52.779 --> 00:13:55.543
Who can do that better than you?


00:13:57.017 --> 00:13:59.815
Tell me. No one, man.


00:13:59.987 --> 00:14:02.512
Look, when this is over,


00:14:02.689 --> 00:14:06.989
Cuba and the revolution
will need you even more.


00:15:33.013 --> 00:15:35.481
They see us rebels as agitators,


00:15:35.715 --> 00:15:39.674
people who want to gain prestige
by complicating Batista's life.


00:15:39.853 --> 00:15:41.480
But we don't see ourselves like that.


00:15:42.222 --> 00:15:45.487
We see ourselves as a small army
that will become a bigger army...


00:15:45.992 --> 00:15:50.326
Fidel has to be the commander in chief
of the entire rebellion.


00:15:52.132 --> 00:15:55.363
But we have to propose it with tact.


00:15:56.002 --> 00:16:00.632
Our relationship with the Communist Party
still makes people nervous.


00:16:01.408 --> 00:16:06.141
We raised funds by naming Fidel


00:16:06.313 --> 00:16:09.146
as leader of our revolution.


00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:14.587
Outside of Cuba, he's the only
recognizable figure we've got.


00:16:14.988 --> 00:16:19.220
No one is saying that in the plains
they screwed up.


00:16:19.392 --> 00:16:21.553
But what is clear
in the Sierra Maestra


00:16:21.728 --> 00:16:25.892
is that defeating Batista doesn't
assure the end of the dictatorship.


00:16:26.066 --> 00:16:29.229
We also have to overthrow
Batista's army


00:16:29.402 --> 00:16:31.996
in order to prevent another coup.


00:16:32.672 --> 00:16:35.004
Being under the command
of the Soviet Union


00:16:35.175 --> 00:16:38.872
isn't any better than being under
the command of the United States.


00:16:39.179 --> 00:16:43.206
Latour, you're still thinking
like a colonized person does.


00:16:43.383 --> 00:16:46.284
Cuba won't be under
anyone's command.


00:16:47.254 --> 00:16:49.688
Cuba is for the Cuban people.


00:16:50.357 --> 00:16:54.225
I'll do everything I can
with the Stalinists from the PSP,


00:16:54.394 --> 00:16:56.385
but I don't think it will be worth it.


00:17:00.066 --> 00:17:02.557
And we understand it, Faustino.


00:17:02.736 --> 00:17:05.330
That's precisely why
we always want to include...


00:17:05.505 --> 00:17:07.405
"Stalinists"?


00:17:08.542 --> 00:17:13.206
From now on, the coordination
of the plains militias


00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:18.977
will serve the needs
of the guerrillas in the Sierra Maestra.


00:17:19.152 --> 00:17:23.555
Fidel Castro will become commander
in chief of all the armed forces.


00:17:25.425 --> 00:17:27.450
Long live the revolution!


00:17:41.341 --> 00:17:43.400
I want to congratulate you, Fidel,


00:17:44.344 --> 00:17:47.711
because today you entered the path
of the greatest men of the Americas.


00:17:49.683 --> 00:17:51.651
A path that


00:17:52.485 --> 00:17:54.419
will prove to the world


00:17:55.789 --> 00:17:59.987
it's possible to get to power
with an armed struggle


00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.151
supported by the people.


00:18:05.465 --> 00:18:07.262
It's not only me, Ernesto.


00:18:07.867 --> 00:18:09.596
It's all of us.


00:18:09.769 --> 00:18:13.535
This wouldn't be possible
if I were on my own.


00:18:17.811 --> 00:18:20.006
I want you to organize a new front.


00:18:21.615 --> 00:18:23.082
Once we start this offensive,


00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:25.980
I want to take the war down
from the Sierra Maestra into the plains.


00:18:29.089 --> 00:18:32.149
You'll have to unite
all the rebel factions.


00:18:32.892 --> 00:18:37.454
We have to take control of Las Villas
Province, dividing the island in two.


00:18:37.831 --> 00:18:41.995
Camilo's going to head in the same
direction, leading his own column.


00:18:44.871 --> 00:18:47.237
There will be no victory in Havana


00:18:47.841 --> 00:18:49.968
without victory in Las Villas.


00:18:52.345 --> 00:18:56.577
Getting all the groups to work together
will be difficult, Ernesto.


00:18:56.750 --> 00:19:00.242
So I hope you have sharpened
your political skills.


00:19:03.823 --> 00:19:05.256
And one other thing.


00:19:05.625 --> 00:19:07.684
I know you are very reckless,


00:19:08.061 --> 00:19:11.155
but you can't always
put yourself on the frontline.


00:19:11.631 --> 00:19:13.758
You are too important to us.


00:19:14.067 --> 00:19:15.694
It's an order.


00:19:25.445 --> 00:19:27.913
I want to respond
to the Nicaraguan delegate


00:19:28.081 --> 00:19:32.711
even though I did not understand
his argument about accent.


00:19:33.453 --> 00:19:36.513
I believe he referred to Cuba,


00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:41.850
Argentina and somewhat
to Russia of the Soviet Union.


00:19:42.462 --> 00:19:44.191
In any event,


00:19:44.364 --> 00:19:49.597
I hope the Nicaraguan delegate found
no North American accent in my speech,


00:19:49.969 --> 00:19:52.733
because that would be truly dangerous.


00:19:53.173 --> 00:19:56.574
But one thing is for sure,
we don't commit assassinations


00:19:56.743 --> 00:19:59.769
like the ones being committed
right at this moment


00:19:59.946 --> 00:20:04.315
by the political police of Venezuela
who are called DIGEPOL


00:20:04.484 --> 00:20:06.349
if I am not misinformed.


00:20:06.586 --> 00:20:09.783
This police force has committed
a series of barbarous acts,


00:20:09.956 --> 00:20:13.221
executions,
which is to say assassinations.


00:20:13.393 --> 00:20:15.759
The Panamanian delegate,


00:20:16.062 --> 00:20:18.656
who has been kind enough
to call me "Che"


00:20:18.832 --> 00:20:20.857
as I am called by the Cuban people,


00:20:22.235 --> 00:20:23.930
began speaking
about the Mexican revolution.


00:20:24.104 --> 00:20:28.473
While Cuba spoke about the
North American massacre in Panama,


00:20:28.641 --> 00:20:30.666
the Panamanian delegation


00:20:30.844 --> 00:20:35.247
continued speaking in this vein,
without referring at all


00:20:37.951 --> 00:20:40.511
to that American massacre for which


00:20:40.687 --> 00:20:45.886
the Panamanian government broke off
relations to the United States.


00:20:46.059 --> 00:20:50.223
On to Mr. Stevenson.
Regrettably, he is not present here.


00:20:51.998 --> 00:20:56.458
Mr. Stevenson again claims
there is no violation of the law


00:20:56.636 --> 00:21:01.335
that neither airplanes nor boats
leave from here and, of course,


00:21:01.508 --> 00:21:05.706
that pirate attacks just happen.
They just come out of nowhere.


00:21:07.046 --> 00:21:13.417
Due to the demands of imperialism,
our prime minister declared five points


00:21:13.586 --> 00:21:16.680
to secure peace in the Caribbean.


00:21:16.856 --> 00:21:18.414
And these are...


00:21:18.591 --> 00:21:19.615
First:


00:21:20.126 --> 00:21:25.154
<i>A halt to the economic blockade</i>
<i>and all forms of commercial pressure</i>


00:21:25.331 --> 00:21:30.928
<i>imposed by the United States</i>
<i>all over the world against our country.</i>


00:21:31.104 --> 00:21:34.437
Second: Halt all subversive activities,


00:21:35.008 --> 00:21:39.536
<i>such as the launch and distribution</i>
<i>of arms and explosives by air and water,</i>


00:21:39.712 --> 00:21:42.010
<i>organization of mercenary invasions,</i>


00:21:43.216 --> 00:21:45.343
<i>infiltration of spies and saboteurs,</i>


00:21:45.552 --> 00:21:49.818
<i>and all actions carried out</i>
<i>from the territory of the United States</i>


00:21:49.989 --> 00:21:52.617
<i>or accomplice countries.</i>


00:21:53.393 --> 00:21:54.451
<i>Third:</i>


00:21:54.794 --> 00:21:58.696
<i>Halt all pirate attacks</i>
<i>carried out from bases located</i>


00:21:58.865 --> 00:22:01.800
<i>in the United States and Puerto Rico.</i>


00:22:05.438 --> 00:22:09.807
<i>Fourth: Halt all airspace</i>
<i>and territorial water violations</i>


00:22:09.976 --> 00:22:13.673
<i>by U.S. Aircraft and warships.</i>


00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:17.709
Fifth: Withdrawal from
the Guantánamo naval base


00:22:18.017 --> 00:22:21.544
<i>and return of Cuban territory</i>
<i>occupied by the U.S.</i>


00:22:28.428 --> 00:22:32.455
<i>This great mass of humanity has said</i>
<i>"Enough!" and has stepped forward.</i>


00:22:32.632 --> 00:22:38.366
<i>This march of giants will not stop</i>
<i>until true independence is won,</i>


00:22:38.538 --> 00:22:42.770
<i>for which so many died in vain.</i>


00:22:44.344 --> 00:22:46.608
All of this, my fellow delegates,


00:22:46.779 --> 00:22:50.306
is the new stance
of the American continent,


00:22:50.483 --> 00:22:53.577
a stance captured by the cry


00:22:53.753 --> 00:22:56.813
that is shouted
every day by our people


00:22:56.990 --> 00:23:00.187
as an expression of our
irrefutable decision to fight,


00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:02.988
<i>paralyzing the strikes</i>
<i>of armed intruders,</i>


00:23:03.162 --> 00:23:07.599
<i>an outcry that counts the support</i>
<i>of all the people of the world</i>


00:23:07.800 --> 00:23:12.362
<i>and especially the socialist camp</i>
<i>headed by the Soviet Union.</i>


00:23:12.539 --> 00:23:16.498
This cry is "Homeland or death!"


00:23:35.695 --> 00:23:37.219
Che!


00:23:40.199 --> 00:23:43.293
That's Las Villas, behind the clouds.


00:23:53.446 --> 00:23:56.904
Camilo arrived a few weeks ago
and we put ourselves under his command.


00:23:57.083 --> 00:23:58.607
Very good.


00:23:58.785 --> 00:24:01.879
- I see you received our supplies.
- Yes, thanks.


00:24:02.055 --> 00:24:04.182
Of all the groups operating in the area,


00:24:04.357 --> 00:24:06.985
the Communist Party
was the only one to send help.


00:24:07.160 --> 00:24:08.752
I'm not surprised, comandante.


00:24:08.928 --> 00:24:12.728
Most of these groups
are too busy fighting each other.


00:24:13.032 --> 00:24:18.561
Months ago, Menoyo broke from
the Directory, creating a Second Front.


00:24:18.738 --> 00:24:21.298
Since then, each one has carved out
its own territory.


00:24:21.474 --> 00:24:24.534
There's been open hostility
between the two factions.


00:24:24.711 --> 00:24:28.044
Where does the 26th of July Movement
stand in all of this?


00:24:28.948 --> 00:24:32.179
Recently,
Menoyo met with Víctor Bordón.


00:24:32.352 --> 00:24:35.549
I think both groups


00:24:35.722 --> 00:24:37.781
are on the brink
of an armed confrontation.


00:24:38.324 --> 00:24:41.589
We're ready to cooperate
with the 26th of July Movement


00:24:41.828 --> 00:24:44.558
in all military maneuvers.


00:24:44.731 --> 00:24:48.462
We even agree with agrarian reform


00:24:48.668 --> 00:24:52.866
as long as it's done reasonably


00:24:53.039 --> 00:24:55.735
and brings in money.


00:24:56.776 --> 00:25:00.610
Landowners should be pressured


00:25:01.180 --> 00:25:05.207
to sell their idle land to the peasants.


00:25:05.385 --> 00:25:07.717
But it should be sold at cost.


00:25:08.254 --> 00:25:10.654
Will you be the one fixing the price?


00:25:11.057 --> 00:25:13.582
How can a peasant
with no money buy land?


00:25:15.194 --> 00:25:18.652
But what do you want?
Just give it to them?


00:25:18.831 --> 00:25:21.459
So they can destroy it
like they did in Mexico?


00:25:21.634 --> 00:25:24.432
The owner of the land
is the one who works it.


00:25:25.505 --> 00:25:31.000
Comandante, you have permission
to institute agrarian reform in the region,


00:25:31.277 --> 00:25:35.373
but the Second Front will continue
to charge the land taxes.


00:25:35.715 --> 00:25:40.846
Menoyo, the region belongs to us all.
What we have to do here is fight.


00:25:42.121 --> 00:25:44.589
The only thing the Directory won't do


00:25:44.824 --> 00:25:49.090
is any kind of deal
with Menoyo's Second Front.


00:25:49.262 --> 00:25:52.925
We'll never do business
with that bunch of bandits.


00:25:53.099 --> 00:25:55.897
We need to attack
all the army garrisons in the area.


00:25:56.069 --> 00:25:57.900
But you can't attack
Güinía de Miranda,


00:25:58.071 --> 00:25:59.470
because that zone is ours.


00:25:59.639 --> 00:26:03.666
We have more experience
and more weapons than you do.


00:26:03.843 --> 00:26:07.472
Do you think the Americans are just
going to sit and watch this happen?


00:26:07.647 --> 00:26:09.581
No, man, listen.


00:26:11.751 --> 00:26:17.053
We shouldn't be doing things
so openly.


00:26:19.058 --> 00:26:22.516
So you're one of those who think
we can make a revolution


00:26:22.695 --> 00:26:25.220
behind the backs of the Americans?


00:26:25.565 --> 00:26:30.264
No, man.
A real revolution cannot be hidden.


00:26:30.436 --> 00:26:33.803
I can do more
with the 400 rifles I have


00:26:33.973 --> 00:26:36.965
than you can with your little bazooka


00:26:37.143 --> 00:26:41.512
and all the balls your troops may have.


00:26:42.782 --> 00:26:47.810
Look, Pena, the day I have
to take arms against my comrades


00:26:47.987 --> 00:26:50.455
will be the day I stop fighting.


00:26:51.891 --> 00:26:56.453
If you don't take Güinía de Miranda
in five days, we'll do it ourselves.


00:26:58.698 --> 00:27:01.462
<i>I am Comandante Ernesto Guevara.</i>


00:27:03.703 --> 00:27:06.900
He is Comandante Ramiro Valdés.


00:27:07.240 --> 00:27:10.971
And he is Captain Victor Bordón.


00:27:12.979 --> 00:27:15.777
I just want to say three things.


00:27:16.015 --> 00:27:17.642
First:


00:27:18.184 --> 00:27:23.315
From now on, I am the only one


00:27:23.489 --> 00:27:27.653
in charge of the region of Las Villas.


00:27:28.227 --> 00:27:29.888
Second:


00:27:31.030 --> 00:27:34.022
We will enforce strict discipline.


00:27:36.235 --> 00:27:37.668
And third:


00:27:38.905 --> 00:27:41.465
The fighting is going to intensify.


00:27:43.709 --> 00:27:48.078
Whoever is not ready to sacrifice
himself for his homeland


00:27:48.247 --> 00:27:50.681
can leave his gun on the ground


00:27:51.250 --> 00:27:53.480
and abandon the column


00:27:54.453 --> 00:27:55.977
immediately.


00:28:07.934 --> 00:28:09.094
Fire.


00:28:38.497 --> 00:28:40.362
Give it to me, damn it!


00:28:54.280 --> 00:28:56.475
Homeland or death!


00:29:24.944 --> 00:29:26.241
You're ready?


00:29:35.454 --> 00:29:36.921
Thank you.


00:29:46.465 --> 00:29:49.332
Tell Oltuski the money
will be put to good use.


00:29:49.502 --> 00:29:51.026
Will do.


00:29:54.206 --> 00:29:55.639
Excuse me.


00:29:55.975 --> 00:29:59.604
The police are looking for me
in Santa Clara and want to arrest me.


00:29:59.779 --> 00:30:02.839
I need to stay here.
I'm not going anywhere.


00:30:03.549 --> 00:30:06.985
Well, you can stay
and work in the infirmary,


00:30:07.153 --> 00:30:09.849
because we don't allow people
to just hang around.


00:30:10.990 --> 00:30:13.891
I want you to know that
for the last two years


00:30:14.060 --> 00:30:16.221
I've been working
in the clandestine movement.


00:30:16.395 --> 00:30:20.422
I've been taking weapons, bombs
and fugitives all across the province.


00:30:20.599 --> 00:30:23.659
I think that gives me the right
to become a guerrilla.


00:30:23.936 --> 00:30:25.028
Okay.


00:30:25.204 --> 00:30:28.230
We've started taxing


00:30:28.407 --> 00:30:30.967
some of the largest landowners.


00:30:31.177 --> 00:30:33.907
I need someone to collect the money.


00:30:34.080 --> 00:30:36.981
You can start with that
and then we'll see.


00:30:37.350 --> 00:30:38.817
Thanks.


00:30:39.251 --> 00:30:40.741
Ramiro.


00:30:41.921 --> 00:30:44.719
- The girl here will collect the taxes.
- Okay.


00:31:43.182 --> 00:31:46.276
One machine gun, 180 rifles


00:31:46.452 --> 00:31:48.317
and 9,000 rounds of ammunition.


00:31:49.021 --> 00:31:52.252
Víctor, we need you to blow
the Cabaiguán bridge.


00:31:52.425 --> 00:31:54.518
The Cabaiguán bridge? Now?


00:31:54.693 --> 00:31:56.593
Yes. Now.


00:31:58.998 --> 00:32:00.522
How did it go?


00:32:01.133 --> 00:32:03.101
I couldn't collect the money.


00:32:03.269 --> 00:32:06.170
In Placetas, the police
are looking for me too.


00:32:06.338 --> 00:32:07.828
Rogelio!


00:32:08.007 --> 00:32:09.998
Take the <i>companeras</i> back to camp.


00:32:10.176 --> 00:32:13.441
Wait a minute. With all due respect,


00:32:13.846 --> 00:32:17.942
I know these towns like the back
of my hand. Let me be your guide.


00:32:18.117 --> 00:32:19.744
I already have a guide.


00:32:31.497 --> 00:32:34.989
Don't worry.
I know you're going to stay with us.


00:32:35.167 --> 00:32:38.864
Don't be like that. Calm down, girl.


00:32:40.239 --> 00:32:42.139
Don't worry.


00:32:55.020 --> 00:32:56.749
Do you know Cabaiguán?


00:33:05.865 --> 00:33:09.357
And tell Milián to have his people ready.


00:33:09.535 --> 00:33:11.298
We'll attack the garrison.


00:33:11.470 --> 00:33:13.233
Perfect.


00:33:22.781 --> 00:33:24.078
Che.


00:33:24.250 --> 00:33:26.275
We have to give you a tetanus shot.


00:33:28.354 --> 00:33:31.448
No, it might trigger
an asthma attack.


00:33:31.624 --> 00:33:33.956
Give me some aspirin.


00:33:41.066 --> 00:33:43.694
Comandante, this is
the Virgin of Caridad del Cobre,


00:33:43.869 --> 00:33:46.429
the patron saint of Cuba,
to help your arrival in Havana.


00:33:46.605 --> 00:33:49.472
I hope it helps us arrive in Placetas.


00:33:49.642 --> 00:33:51.439
Goodbye!


00:33:51.877 --> 00:33:55.813
- How are you? Does it hurt?
- A little, but that's unavoidable.


00:33:59.151 --> 00:34:00.812
Here, for your arm.


00:34:01.554 --> 00:34:02.885
Thanks.


00:34:04.323 --> 00:34:06.348
Long live the revolution!


00:34:25.544 --> 00:34:27.944
Shit, Argentine. You broke your paw?


00:34:28.147 --> 00:34:30.843
- It's nothing. I fell off a roof.
- So, what happened?


00:34:31.016 --> 00:34:34.076
- I just spoke to Fidel.
- And?


00:34:34.253 --> 00:34:36.448
Santiago has almost surrendered.


00:34:36.622 --> 00:34:39.022
Santa Clara is the only thing
standing between us and Havana.


00:34:39.191 --> 00:34:42.490
Batista's throwing everything
he's got to Santa Clara.


00:34:42.661 --> 00:34:44.128
That's why,


00:34:44.296 --> 00:34:47.265
when you take Remedios
and I take Yaguajay,


00:34:47.466 --> 00:34:50.333
we can then take
Santa Clara together.


00:34:51.437 --> 00:34:52.995
Give me a light.


00:35:00.479 --> 00:35:02.947
I know what I'm going to do
when we win this thing.


00:35:03.115 --> 00:35:04.639
I'll put you in a cage,


00:35:04.817 --> 00:35:07.615
tour the country and charge admission.


00:35:07.786 --> 00:35:09.845
We'll be rich, man!


00:35:16.662 --> 00:35:18.960
What made you join the Movement?


00:35:19.965 --> 00:35:24.629
Well, I was in college when Fidel
attacked the Moncada Barracks.


00:35:24.803 --> 00:35:28.330
When I read his defense plea,
"History Will Absolve Me,"


00:35:28.507 --> 00:35:31.476
I knew he was the only one
who could take down Batista.


00:35:31.644 --> 00:35:35.307
And that he would do it fighting,
and I liked that.


00:35:35.481 --> 00:35:37.381
Does your family support you?


00:35:37.549 --> 00:35:38.982
Of course.


00:35:39.151 --> 00:35:41.881
My cousin was killed.


00:35:43.055 --> 00:35:47.754
The brutality of the army
intensified after the general strike.


00:35:48.827 --> 00:35:49.987
I think they got scared


00:35:50.195 --> 00:35:53.426
when they saw
so many people against them.


00:35:59.338 --> 00:36:01.431
You don't look like a Communist.


00:36:02.141 --> 00:36:05.577
- And what do Communists look like?
- Well, not like you.


00:36:05.744 --> 00:36:07.541
We come in all colors.


00:36:13.385 --> 00:36:17.116
Do you expect to stay in Cuba
after the success of the revolution?


00:36:17.723 --> 00:36:20.089
My wife and my daughter are in Mexico.


00:36:20.259 --> 00:36:22.523
I have to keep them in mind.


00:36:23.696 --> 00:36:24.958
Of course.


00:36:28.534 --> 00:36:31.560
I'm Lieutenant Pérez Valencia.


00:36:31.737 --> 00:36:33.568
The rebel army


00:36:33.739 --> 00:36:36.037
is not what you have imagined.


00:36:36.208 --> 00:36:38.836
Hand over your weapons
and no one will be injured.


00:36:40.546 --> 00:36:42.446
Stay on the air, over.


00:36:42.781 --> 00:36:44.942
Santa Clara hasn't sent reinforcements.


00:36:45.117 --> 00:36:47.449
It's a lost cause for these people.


00:36:47.886 --> 00:36:49.717
<i>Attention, Che, attention.</i>
<i>Che, attention, Che.</i>


00:36:49.888 --> 00:36:53.984
Listen, could you resolve the problem
and follow the instructions,


00:36:54.159 --> 00:36:57.424
the instructions, the instructions
you gave me with the man I sent?


00:36:57.596 --> 00:37:01.794
<i>So tell me if you understand, understand,</i>
<i>understand me. Over, Che.</i>


00:37:01.967 --> 00:37:04.435
Camilo, I hear you perfectly.


00:37:05.070 --> 00:37:08.471
Your record is broken,
you have to change it. Over.


00:37:09.842 --> 00:37:12.777
How long will you be
in Yaguajay? Over.


00:37:12.945 --> 00:37:15.846
<i>Three days, maybe a week. Over.</i>


00:37:16.014 --> 00:37:18.312
The more time you stay there


00:37:18.517 --> 00:37:21.884
the harder it will be here,
Camilo. Over.


00:37:22.621 --> 00:37:26.216
<i>Don't dare to enter the city</i>
<i>without me, do you hear?</i>


00:37:27.426 --> 00:37:30.657
Camilo, it's fair to share
the glory sometimes. Over.


00:37:30.829 --> 00:37:34.458
Sharing the glory is fine,
but with an Argentine,


00:37:34.633 --> 00:37:36.794
don't do that to me.


00:37:37.302 --> 00:37:39.293
Over and out, Che.


00:37:55.320 --> 00:37:58.653
It's good to have you in Santa Clara,
Colonel Casillas.


00:37:59.324 --> 00:38:02.316
The city's forces are at your disposal.


00:38:03.128 --> 00:38:05.961
Can those forces
get me some coffee?


00:38:06.398 --> 00:38:09.060
The best beans in the world, colonel.


00:38:15.174 --> 00:38:16.471
Sit down.


00:39:30.582 --> 00:39:32.675
<i>People of Santa Clara,</i>


00:39:32.851 --> 00:39:35.820
<i>this is Comandante Guevara speaking.</i>


00:39:36.955 --> 00:39:39.549
<i>The enemy wants us to live in fear,</i>


00:39:39.725 --> 00:39:41.693
<i>but it is they who should be afraid.</i>


00:39:43.629 --> 00:39:47.588
<i>The situation of the military regime</i>
<i>is getting worse every day,</i>


00:39:48.767 --> 00:39:51.099
<i>because their soldiers</i>
<i>don't want to fight.</i>


00:39:54.773 --> 00:39:56.001
<i>Santa Clara,</i>


00:39:56.775 --> 00:40:02.008
<i>if there has ever been a time</i>
<i>to fight for our freedom,</i>


00:40:02.180 --> 00:40:05.115
<i>that time is now.</i>


00:40:05.284 --> 00:40:08.151
That moment has come.


00:40:24.169 --> 00:40:26.262
I want air strikes


00:40:27.205 --> 00:40:29.469
all around the neighborhoods.


00:40:30.776 --> 00:40:32.903
Torch those bastards!


00:41:06.678 --> 00:41:08.441
He's dead.


00:41:11.183 --> 00:41:12.673
Cover him with that sheet.


00:41:12.851 --> 00:41:14.443
I need more help.


00:41:14.853 --> 00:41:16.320
- Aleida.
- The situation is critical.


00:41:16.521 --> 00:41:19.388
Talk to Camajuani
and ask for more doctors.


00:42:11.943 --> 00:42:13.103
Yes?


00:42:14.046 --> 00:42:17.243
Comandante, it's Rogelio
calling from the station.


00:42:21.453 --> 00:42:22.477
Speak to me, Rogelio.


00:42:22.654 --> 00:42:26.886
Comandante, we took the train station.


00:42:27.125 --> 00:42:28.820
Is it safe?


00:42:30.095 --> 00:42:31.221
Good.


00:42:31.396 --> 00:42:36.299
Go with 15 men to the train tracks
between Toscano and San Pedro


00:42:36.468 --> 00:42:38.436
and wait there.


00:42:38.670 --> 00:42:40.035
All right.


00:43:40.332 --> 00:43:43.324
The tank is screwing us.
The machine gun doesn't let us get closer.


00:43:43.502 --> 00:43:44.696
For Guile and Ramiro.


00:43:44.870 --> 00:43:47.304
- What's the highest position?
- The church at the end of the street.


00:43:47.472 --> 00:43:49.770
Then you have to take the church,
you must take the church.


00:43:49.941 --> 00:43:51.499
Of course, comandante.


00:43:54.112 --> 00:43:55.409
Go.


00:44:07.359 --> 00:44:08.758
Hit it hard.


00:44:17.202 --> 00:44:19.670
- How many houses do we have to cross?
- Five.


00:44:20.872 --> 00:44:23.272
Little Cowboy, it's too many.


00:44:25.010 --> 00:44:27.945
Hit it hard.
Fuck. We have to break it down now!


00:45:40.151 --> 00:45:43.120
Get down, Little Cowboy.
You're going to get hit.


00:46:05.143 --> 00:46:06.474
Stay here.


00:46:51.723 --> 00:46:53.213
Aleida!


00:47:11.843 --> 00:47:14.835
- What the fuck are you doing?
- The SIM is on the hotel rooftop.


00:47:15.814 --> 00:47:17.805
They hit Little Cowboy.


00:47:20.819 --> 00:47:23.379
Tamayo. What happened?


00:47:25.890 --> 00:47:27.357
They got Little Cowboy, comandante.


00:47:27.525 --> 00:47:28.958
What happened to him?


00:47:29.127 --> 00:47:31.960
We claimed a rooftop
to get a good position,


00:47:32.630 --> 00:47:36.726
and then he got shot in the head.
They killed him.


00:47:46.044 --> 00:47:47.875
Take him to the medical station.


00:47:55.220 --> 00:47:56.551
Tamayo.


00:47:57.088 --> 00:47:59.488
You are now in charge
of the suicide platoon.


00:47:59.791 --> 00:48:02.760
Keep breaking the walls
until you reach the church.


00:48:02.927 --> 00:48:04.519
They need to pay for this.


00:48:15.673 --> 00:48:20.372
The rebels have surrounded the city
and our tanks can't cross the barricades.


00:48:21.246 --> 00:48:22.645
Shit.


00:48:26.484 --> 00:48:28.679
Get Havana on the phone.


00:48:30.688 --> 00:48:33.350
Tell them to airlift men
from Cienfuegos.


00:48:35.660 --> 00:48:38.652
We're going to secure this city
neighborhood by neighborhood


00:48:38.830 --> 00:48:40.889
and street by street.


00:48:42.000 --> 00:48:43.024
Send a battalion.


00:49:59.010 --> 00:50:00.238
Where are you going?


00:50:00.411 --> 00:50:03.710
I don't want to fight anymore.
I'm tired of this.


00:50:05.583 --> 00:50:07.107
Let me go.


00:50:14.225 --> 00:50:16.420
Anyone else want to leave?


00:50:20.431 --> 00:50:22.592
Cease fire!


00:50:23.368 --> 00:50:25.427
Cease fire!


00:50:44.322 --> 00:50:46.882
Tell your men to put down their arms.


00:50:47.091 --> 00:50:49.582
I'm not going to negotiate
with a subordinate.


00:50:50.528 --> 00:50:52.496
You forgot to leave your gun.


00:50:52.664 --> 00:50:56.191
- Give me that gun.
- Take your belt off.


00:50:58.937 --> 00:51:02.304
I said I wouldn't negotiate
with a subordinate.


00:51:02.473 --> 00:51:05.909
That's okay. This isn't a negotiation.


00:51:06.811 --> 00:51:08.438
Comandante,


00:51:08.746 --> 00:51:11.476
I give you my word of honor that
if you let us return to Havana,


00:51:11.649 --> 00:51:13.913
we won't fire another shot.


00:51:14.085 --> 00:51:16.383
I believe your word of honor.


00:51:16.554 --> 00:51:20.854
But I can't let those bullets kill more
Cubans. Here or anywhere else.


00:51:21.593 --> 00:51:25.427
You have 15 minutes
to convince your men to surrender.


00:51:25.597 --> 00:51:29.966
If not, you will be responsible
for any bloodshed.


00:51:37.208 --> 00:51:39.199
Shit!


00:51:42.880 --> 00:51:45.542
Send this box to Camilo in Yaguajay.


00:51:45.717 --> 00:51:48.083
Aleida, come here.


00:52:20.718 --> 00:52:22.413
Call them on the telephone.


00:52:24.355 --> 00:52:29.292
We agree to a ceasefire
to get our dead and wounded.


00:52:36.234 --> 00:52:39.397
- I advise you to surrender.
- Over my dead body.


00:52:40.905 --> 00:52:43.669
What's wrong with you?
Where are you going?


00:52:49.280 --> 00:52:52.044
Your colonel wants you
to fight to the death.


00:52:54.218 --> 00:52:57.278
We don't want more Cubans to die.


00:52:58.723 --> 00:53:00.748
Give up your weapons


00:53:01.559 --> 00:53:03.550
and you will live.


00:53:08.700 --> 00:53:10.463
Turn in your weapons!


00:53:11.436 --> 00:53:12.926
Now!


00:53:30.955 --> 00:53:32.388
Well...


00:53:34.125 --> 00:53:36.218
The colonel and I


00:53:36.461 --> 00:53:40.864
are going on a special mission
to check our positions.


00:53:42.300 --> 00:53:45.599
Keep up the resistance
until I return, is that clear?


00:53:45.770 --> 00:53:47.761
Whatever you say, colonel.


00:53:51.008 --> 00:53:53.135
Shoot anyone who tries to leave.


00:54:07.325 --> 00:54:08.656
Who is this?


00:54:08.826 --> 00:54:11.693
That's Sánchez, the police captain.


00:54:12.630 --> 00:54:15.292
We found torture instruments
in the station.


00:54:22.106 --> 00:54:25.439
You know,
I have an idea to take the hotel.


00:54:26.844 --> 00:54:28.368
Tell me.


00:54:28.546 --> 00:54:30.104
Leave it to me.


00:55:38.115 --> 00:55:41.050
Don't shoot, don't shoot!
We surrender!


00:55:41.919 --> 00:55:43.716
Turn in your weapons!


00:55:54.832 --> 00:55:56.629
Come on, hurry up!


00:56:12.884 --> 00:56:16.843
Camilo took Yaguajay and he
and his troops are heading this way.


00:56:17.855 --> 00:56:20.119
We just heard the news
on the shortwave.


00:56:20.291 --> 00:56:22.851
It looks like Batista
abandoned the country.


00:56:24.929 --> 00:56:27.022
Yes, sir. Right now.


00:56:33.371 --> 00:56:36.499
It's General Cantillo
calling from Havana.


00:56:38.175 --> 00:56:39.733
Okay, leave.


00:56:41.779 --> 00:56:42.837
Yes, general?


00:56:43.014 --> 00:56:48.316
<i>I'm negotiating directly with</i>
<i>the U.S. Ambassador.</i>


00:56:48.519 --> 00:56:53.149
<i>I'm in command of the army now,</i>
<i>acting on behalf of Fidel Castro.</i>


00:56:53.324 --> 00:56:57.658
<i>I authorize you to negotiate a truce,</i>
<i>but not to surrender.</i>


00:56:57.828 --> 00:57:01.127
<i>You can't surrender</i>
<i>under any circumstances.</i>


00:57:02.099 --> 00:57:04.033
As you say, general.


00:57:07.838 --> 00:57:09.465
Captain.


00:57:09.774 --> 00:57:11.503
I need to talk to Guevara.


00:57:13.277 --> 00:57:17.714
<i>I've spoken to Fidel Castro. There's</i>
<i>been no deal with General Cantillo.</i>


00:57:18.916 --> 00:57:22.147
This is a revolution, not a coup.


00:57:22.320 --> 00:57:27.758
It's either unconditional surrender
or we'll take the garrison by force.


00:57:27.959 --> 00:57:30.689
And you'll be responsible
for the bloodshed.


00:57:30.928 --> 00:57:35.297
Be aware of the possibility that
the U.S. Government will intervene


00:57:35.466 --> 00:57:37.331
militarily in Cuba.


00:57:37.535 --> 00:57:41.437
If that happens,
it would be an even bigger crime,


00:57:41.939 --> 00:57:44.737
as you will be supporting
a foreign invasion.


00:57:45.676 --> 00:57:47.803
In that case, your only
remaining option would be


00:57:47.979 --> 00:57:51.312
for you to shoot yourself
for committing treason.


00:57:52.383 --> 00:57:56.080
Mr. Guevara, I need to talk
with my superiors about that.


00:57:59.223 --> 00:58:01.555
It's 19 minutes past 10.


00:58:02.059 --> 00:58:07.122
At 11, I'll give the order to attack
using all our forces.


00:58:21.112 --> 00:58:25.014
- Sir, may I return home to my family?
- No.


00:58:25.182 --> 00:58:27.082
But we won the revolution already!


00:58:27.251 --> 00:58:30.914
We only won the war,
the revolution begins now.


00:58:37.094 --> 00:58:40.552
Get all your things,
we're leaving for Havana tomorrow.


00:58:40.731 --> 00:58:42.528
Aleida. You too.


00:58:42.700 --> 00:58:44.827
I'll need a guide.


00:58:45.002 --> 00:58:48.733
- But I don't know Havana very well.
- Neither do I.


00:58:51.909 --> 00:58:55.936
- This man wants to say hello to you.
- Thanks for all you've done for Cuba.


00:58:56.113 --> 00:59:00.243
Not me, all of them. All of them.


00:59:03.320 --> 00:59:06.983
Get ready.
We're leaving for Havana tomorrow.


00:59:17.501 --> 00:59:20.334
He told me he was heading to Havana
to participate in a military junta


00:59:20.504 --> 00:59:23.667
which was going to resolve
the problems of the Cuban people.


00:59:23.841 --> 00:59:27.902
I told him murderers like him weren't
going to resolve anything anymore.


00:59:28.412 --> 00:59:30.073
When I told him
I was bringing him to you,


00:59:30.247 --> 00:59:32.408
he pissed in his pants.


00:59:32.583 --> 00:59:35.347
He begged me
to take him to another chief.


00:59:35.820 --> 00:59:37.515
What do you want me
to do with this guy?


00:59:37.688 --> 00:59:41.988
Keep him as a prisoner of war.
He will be judged by a tribunal.


00:59:42.593 --> 00:59:45.289
Comandante, place him
under special watch.


00:59:45.463 --> 00:59:46.953
Sure.


00:59:49.834 --> 00:59:52.302
- Son of a bitch.
- Bandit.


00:59:52.970 --> 00:59:54.494
I can't see anything,
then I turn around


00:59:54.672 --> 00:59:58.938
and I see Roberto in the jeep,
holding the grenade


00:59:59.110 --> 01:00:01.044
with the pin still in it.


01:00:01.212 --> 01:00:02.270
You're kidding.


01:00:02.446 --> 01:00:05.779
So he's looking at me, smiling,
like I'm stupid.


01:00:05.950 --> 01:00:08.817
But when he came out of the jeep,
I swear to you,


01:00:08.986 --> 01:00:10.783
he stood up,
acting like a tough guy,


01:00:10.988 --> 01:00:14.549
still holding the grenade in his hand,
just like this, boy.


01:00:14.725 --> 01:00:18.126
He could barely walk because
his knees were shaking so hard,


01:00:18.295 --> 01:00:22.994
and suddenly his eyes went up,


01:00:23.167 --> 01:00:27.900
and then he fainted with the grenade
in his hand with the pin still in it.


01:00:29.306 --> 01:00:30.933
Good one.


01:00:38.349 --> 01:00:40.180
Who has a light?


01:00:40.417 --> 01:00:42.282
Not me.


01:00:46.157 --> 01:00:48.022
Hey, this was mine!


01:00:52.630 --> 01:00:55.155
- Gentlemen.
- So, then?


01:00:55.332 --> 01:00:58.233
I'm going to the capital.
Thanks for everything.


01:00:58.435 --> 01:01:01.097
- See you in Havana.
- Of course.


01:01:02.173 --> 01:01:03.435
Ernesto.


01:01:13.284 --> 01:01:15.980
- Take care.
- Yes, Che.


01:01:16.153 --> 01:01:18.314
Don't worry, my man.


01:02:19.850 --> 01:02:21.374
So, then?


01:02:22.019 --> 01:02:23.748
Are you coming with us?


01:02:25.089 --> 01:02:27.922
Yes. Under one condition.


01:02:28.092 --> 01:02:29.320
Which?


01:02:29.493 --> 01:02:31.461
When we're done in Cuba,


01:02:31.629 --> 01:02:34.689
you let me bring the revolution
to all Latin America.


01:02:36.133 --> 01:02:38.727
You, too, are a little crazy.


01:02:44.742 --> 01:02:46.937
It's a thing that I haven't seen
anybody doing.


01:02:47.111 --> 01:02:50.103
The rice is the most important thing,
if you take--


01:02:52.249 --> 01:02:56.549
Comandante,
do you need my services tonight?


01:02:57.955 --> 01:03:00.719
Son, you're killing me.


01:03:00.891 --> 01:03:04.383
Did I make you angry
with what I said the other night?


01:03:04.561 --> 01:03:08.224
I'm sorry,
I don't know what I was thinking.


01:03:10.134 --> 01:03:14.537
No, son, you are loved,
as they say in Cuba.


01:03:14.705 --> 01:03:17.401
- Thank you, comandante.
- Do what you need to do.


01:03:17.574 --> 01:03:19.098
Good night.


01:04:00.351 --> 01:04:02.546
See you in Havana!


01:04:02.920 --> 01:04:04.387
It's Rogelio.


01:04:04.555 --> 01:04:06.182
Tell him to stop.


01:04:07.458 --> 01:04:09.221
- What?
- Rogelio.


01:04:09.426 --> 01:04:10.723
Yes, tell him to stop.


01:04:14.398 --> 01:04:16.662
What are you doing with that car?


01:04:16.867 --> 01:04:18.334
I'm driving it to Havana.


01:04:18.502 --> 01:04:20.094
Who gave you authorization?


01:04:20.604 --> 01:04:24.404
I took it. It belonged
to one of the snipers, man.


01:04:24.575 --> 01:04:26.440
Don't "man" me, Rogelio.


01:04:26.610 --> 01:04:30.671
Even if it was Batista's,
this car isn't yours.


01:04:32.049 --> 01:04:35.746
Go back to Santa Clara immediately
and give it back.


01:04:35.919 --> 01:04:41.255
And then you will go to Havana
by bus, by jeep or on foot.


01:04:41.859 --> 01:04:44.919
I'd rather walk than drive to Havana
in a stolen car. Let's go.


01:05:09.153 --> 01:05:10.984
Unbelievable.

